{
  "prompt": "Explain the role of non-linearities (like ReLU) and how stacking multiple layers allows a neural network to perform complex tasks beyond simple linear classification.",
  "reference_answer": "A neural network requires a non-linear function, $g(z)$, because it is not enough to just use linear combinations of inputs. Non-linearities allow the network to map outputs in a way that is not just a plane, enabling it to learn complex patterns. While a single-layer perceptron can perform linear classification if the data is linearly separable, stacking layers allows the network to build more complex representations. Each subsequent layer applies a non-linearity to the output of the previous layer, allowing the model to learn increasingly intricate features.",
