  "reference_answer": "To approximate a ramp function, one would need to combine and manipulate ReLU functions, similar to how the rectangle was constructed. The basic ReLU shape must be translated and scaled to achieve the desired linear segment. By inserting a constant $c$, which is used to increase the slope of the curves, and then translating the resulting function, the network can be tuned to converge to the target function. This process demonstrates the power of combining ReLUs to create complex shapes.",
