  "reference_answer": "The optimal set of parameters ($\\theta^*$) is the set that is optimal for some cost function, which is the sum of the loss over all training data points. When using gradient descent to find this optimal value, we start on the loss landscape and move in the direction of the gradient to find a minimum. However, if the loss landscape is non-convex and complex, the minimum found may not be guaranteed to be the global minimum. Instead, it might just be a local minimum, and we often do not know how bad that local minimum is relative to the global minimum.",
